    "description": "In this video, Chef John shows you how to make Greek-style beef stew, stifado. The recipe calls for a beef chuck roast that's cut into 2-inch pieces, seasoned with black pepper and kosher salt, and refrigerated until ready to use. Shallots, peeled and kept whole, are browned in Greek olive oil after the beef has been browned in batches. The caramelized meat juices on the bottom of the pan create an amazing fond, which is enhanced by tossing the shallots around the pan until they get a little bit of color on the outsides. This dinner dish is a must-try for any beef stew lover.",
